// "Marais Mitaine": a marsh in the misty morning, its causeways between the reeds and the
// boathouses (issue #112, the 15th circuit, the third of the fourth cup), after the guide
// « Conception des circuits » (docs/GAME_DESIGN.md § 16). Original layout, about 1650 m a lap,
// turning left, from -2 to 14 m up: the start straight on the main causeway, 14 m up; the S of
// the boathouses, two hairpins of 180° back to back (left, right); north to the risky jump's corner (a tight corner to
// the left, its inside a drop, that a ramp crosses), its wide landing, west, and the glide ramp:
// the glide down over the marsh, 11 m; a hairpin to the left, and the ford, east, through the
// water; then the lacets back up through the marsh, three hairpins (right, left, right) and their
// legs, gentle (8 % at most): a trick ramp, a bump, the drop of 4 m off the last leg (36 m after
// its hairpin, 35 m straight below it), the bison; two tight corners to the
// left (south, then east); the bulge round a giant willow, whose hidden road runs straight behind
// a stack of crates; the last corner, that the grass bridge crosses behind a curtain of reeds. Six hairpins of 180° (a Normal bot drifts them), the
// bulge's S (right 75°, left 150°, right 75°), four tight corners of 90°: no long soft curve, one
// long straight. No anti-gravity: the glider and the water instead.
//
// The pieces: the jump's corner, its landing and the
// glide, and the bulge, the last corner and their paths, are the Falaises Flanelle's (the
// Corniche Cannelle's, mirrored: their gains and their hiding were tuned), lower, with other
// covers; the rest is new (the S, the ford and the lacets). Drawn as a plan of straights and arcs
// (hairpins of 22 m, tight corners of 18 m), its points every 8 m along it (the parameters below
// follow them). The generator is not in the repository.
//
// Format: see src/track/data.rs. Point 0 is the start line; karts drive toward point 1 (north,
// -Z), then turn left. The grid sits on the straight behind point 0.
(
    name: "Marais Mitaine",
    // Dressing (issue #11): the marsh in the misty morning (`assets/data/biomes.ron`, Kenney's
    // Watercraft Kit and the Nature Kit), the same every time (seed), and pieces placed by hand:
    // checkered flags at the start line; boathouses along the main causeway; a sailing boat run
    // aground by the jump's corner; a giant willow in the bulge.
    biome: "Marais",
    // Issue #104: its music (`assets/data/music.ron`).
    music: "fairy-adventure",
    decor_seed: 115,
    // Issue #195: the marsh's low banks (`assets/data/biomes.ron`), and they hug the road
    // (`embank`, rise over run: about 31°): the causeways, up to 14 m above the marsh, are carried
    // by the banks up to their walls. The voids stay (the jump's corner, the glide's drop, the
    // bulge, the last corner); the ford keeps its ground.
    terrain: (height: 20.0, scale: 140.0, floor: 0.3, rock: (0.46, 0.40, 0.30), embank: 0.6),
    props: [
        (model: "racing-kit/flagCheckers", at: 0.0, side: Both, height: 4.0, radius: 0.9, gap: 1.8),
        // Boathouses along the main causeway, on the start straight.
        (model: "watercraft-kit/boat-house-a", at: 2.5, side: Right, height: 5.0, radius: 3.0, gap: 0.5),
        (model: "watercraft-kit/boat-house-b", at: 6.0, side: Right, height: 5.0, radius: 3.0, gap: 0.5),
        (model: "watercraft-kit/boat-house-c", at: 2.0, side: Left, height: 5.0, radius: 3.0, gap: 0.5),
        // A sailing boat run aground by the jump's corner, over the marsh.
        (model: "watercraft-kit/boat-sail-a", at: 35.204, side: Right, height: 16.0, radius: 6.0, gap: 2.0),
        // A giant willow in the bulge.
        (model: "nature-kit/tree_detailed_dark", at: 174.216, side: Left, height: 22.0, radius: 3.8, gap: 8.0),
    ],
    checkpoint_spacing: 25.0,
